-- title:
--   Igusa lifting on both j-charts
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ (with `NeZero N`), a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$), a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$, and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$. Write $j=$ `jqModC` for the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}E_4^3\eta^{-24}$ of the modular invariant in $K((q))$ and $j_N=$ `jqNModC` for its substitution $q\mapsto q^N$; `modularFunctionFieldC k N` is the intermediate field $k(\bar j,\bar j_N)\subset k((q))$ generated by these two series, `modularLocalized N A red` is the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ of those $f$ with $fs=r$ for some $r,s$ in the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with $j$ and $j_N$, $s$ outside the prime `redKer` of that subring, and `modularRedLocHom N A red` is the induced reduction homomorphism from this subring to $k((q))$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions. First: every $y\in k(\bar j,\bar j_N)$ which is a root of a monic polynomial in $k[\bar j][Y]$, i.e. for which there is a monic $P\in k[X][Y]$ with $P(y)=0$ after evaluating inner coefficients at $\bar j$ via `Polynomial.eval₂RingHom (algebraMap k (LaurentSeries k)) (jqModC k)`, is the image under `modularRedLocHom N A red` of some $f$ in `modularLocalized N A red` which is likewise a root of a monic polynomial in $A[X][Y]$ with inner coefficients evaluated at $j$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Second: the same statement with $\bar j$ replaced throughout by $\bar j^{-1}$ and $j$ by $j^{-1}$, the inverses taken in the respective Laurent series fields.
--
--   This is Igusa's good-reduction statement for the modular function field of level $N$ at a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above a prime $\ell\nmid N$, in the form of a lifting property on the two affine $j$-charts: integral elements in characteristic $\ell$ come from integral elements in characteristic zero with the same reduction. It feeds the construction of the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre model, in particular the identification of specialised places and of the specialisation of Hecke divisors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_exists_integral_lift_jChart_and_jInvChart.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_CharPReduction

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
